    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0165" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6847/1–2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador of Austria-Hungary to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Austro-Hungarian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1156.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge,
                    with thanks, the receipt of your valued communication, No. 257, of the 8th
                    instant, and to append hereto a corrected list<anchor n="a" xml:id="d52-f1"/> of
                    the districts and incumbents of imperial and royal consular offices in the
                    United States and its insular possessions.</p>
                <p>I have to add, at the same time, that my Government has received no complaint of
                    the character described in my note, No. 1087, of the 23d [30th] ultimo from the
                    consular officers in Porto Rico, Hawaii, and the Philippine Islands.</p>
                <p>Accept, excellency, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hengelmuller.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
